{"format":"tvf-scene","v":1,"name":"example · A square wave from sines","loop":21.1,"ease":"inout","hold":0,"gravity":1,"wind":0,"trail":null,"camera":[],"stops":[0.1327,0.2986,0.5829],"beats":[{"title":"A square wave","text":"A [square wave](#lit:1): up, down, up, down, with a jump between. No smooth curve has a jump in it."},{"title":"One sine","text":"Start with [one sine](#lit:2) of the same length. It is the right way up in the right places, and nothing like square."},{"title":"Add the odd harmonics","text":"Add [a sine](#lit:4) three times as fast and a third as tall, then one five times as fast and a fifth as tall. Each one flattens the tops a little more and steepens the sides."},{"title":"And more","text":"With 5, 9 and 20 the tops are nearly flat. But beside each jump [the sum](#lit:2) still stands above the wave: by 9.1%, 9.0% and 9.0% of the jump. More sines make that ear narrower, not shorter; it settles near 9.0% and stays."}],"path":null,"items":[{"fill":{"color":"#f4f1ea","opacity":1},"stroke":null,"width":0,"open":false,"exact":{"x":[-0.9,0.9,0.9,-0.9],"y":[0.56,0.56,-0.56,-0.56],"r":null,"smooth":null,"ctrl":null,"holes":[]}},{"morph":0},{"morph":1},{"morph":2},{"morph":3},{"morph":4},{"morph":5},{"morph":11},{"morph":12},{"morph":13},{"morph":14},{"morph":15},{"morph":6},{"morph":16},{"morph":17},{"morph":18},{"morph":19},{"morph":20},{"morph":21},{"morph":7},{"morph":22},{"morph":23},{"morph":24},{"morph":25},{"morph":26},{"morph":27},{"morph":8},{"morph":28},{"morph":29},{"morph":30},{"morph":31},{"morph":32},{"morph":33},{"morph":9},{"morph":34},{"morph":35},{"morph":36},{"morph":37},{"morph":38},{"morph":39},{"morph":10},{"morph":40},{"morph":41},{"morph":42},{"morph":43},{"morph":44},{"morph":45},{"morph":46}],"morphs":[{"exact":true,"open":true,"holes":null,"keys":[{"x":[-0.76,0.76],"y":[0.14,0.14],"r":[0,0],"c":[null,null]}],"fill":null,"inPlace":true,"lag":0,"fx":null,"own":{"parent":-1,"parentAt":null,"follow":null,"look":-1,"lookRef":0,"